The Lamp
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/foundry]

FIXME(mundane): Just inside, in the first dark, the man searches a supply closet and hands the PC a carbide lamp. "You'll want this. I won't." He gives his name then, Suhail, as though it had only just occurred to him they had not been introduced.
FIXME(mundane): The PC asks whether he is someone important. He allows that he is, or was. He was brothers with most of the men who run the Kesharat now; rode with them, got into the kind of trouble young men get into, in the good years when they were all young together. "A long time ago. They chose a different path." He still likes trouble. He just does it alone now.
FIXME(dread): He is filthy and sun-baked, dust in every seam of him, and not a day past his mid-thirties under all of it. The arithmetic of "a long time ago" does not sit right against the face saying it, and he offers nothing to fix the discrepancy.
FIXME(dread): He turns, and in the lightless room the Color is the only thing the PC can see of him: his eyes, intense with it, the same purple beyond purple from the scrub now burning behind a living face. Out in the glare it never registered. Here it is unmistakable. He names it before it becomes a question. Kesharat privilege, he calls it, the locals' word for the standing he carries. "Reserved for those the Lattice takes a particular interest in." He moves through the dark at ease. The PC has a circle of lamplight six feet wide.

choices:

* Go deeper into the factory = Follow his lamp-less ease into the dark
    FIXME(dread): The corridor gives out onto the open floor of the place, and the lamp finds no walls. The dark speaks from three directions at once.
    +open "The Factory Floor"
